-- LICENSE SCREEN  (step 1 of 3: License -> Loading -> Arcy UI)
-- Layout numbers, texts and asset ids are the UI source's StartingScreen: user avatar + name (UserPFP2 / StartingNickname),
-- "Welcome to" / title / description, the EmailBox, START + SUBSCRIBE (asset 87886886705009) and the Arceus art (StartingLogo).
-- It is drawn on the loading screen's own glow, so license -> loading is one continuous screen.
--
-- NOTE: there is NO server check in here. START accepts only the emails in LoadingScreen.LICENSE.Allowed (not case sensitive; set Allowed = nil to accept any
-- well-formed email, the same format test as the source) and remembers the accepted email in ArcyScripts/_license.json. For your own check set
-- LoadingScreen.LICENSE.Validate = function(email) return true | false, "message" end (it may yield, e.g. to call your own web api; it replaces Allowed).
-- This is a check inside a client script: anybody who can edit the script can remove it, so it keeps honest users in line, it is not real protection.
-- Tapping the Email box opens the "Instant code with Arcy" search bar (LICENSE.PromptTitle / LICENSE.PromptHint); the typed text goes into the Email box.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
